# The served demo is published as the byte-exact file generated by make_demo.py
# in adamsdarin/dd254-interactive-source, and its SHA-256 is recorded in that
# release. Git must not translate it on checkout: with core.autocrlf on, a fresh
# clone rewrites every LF to CRLF, changes the bytes and makes a local
# comparison against the release fail for a reason that has nothing to do with
# the file's contents. Pages serves the stored blob, so this protects the local
# copy and anyone verifying it.
index.html -text
*.HTM -text
*.html -text
